# Preview Environments

## Intent
Document how preview environments work across Vercel (web app), Railway (realtime service), ensuring all services are properly linked for PR testing.

## Architecture

```
┌────────────────────────────────────┐
│            Pull Request            │
└────────────────────────────────────┘
                   │
        ┌─────────────────────┐
        ▼                     ▼
┌───────────────┐    ┌───────────────┐
│ Vercel Preview│    │Railway Preview│
│  (apps/web)   │◄───│(apps/realtime)│
│               │    │               │
│  API_URL ─────┼────┤               │
└───────────────┘    └───────────────┘
```

## How It Works

### Production (main branch)
1. **Push to main** → Vercel creates production deployment
2. **Vercel deployment succeeds** → GitHub Actions workflow triggers (`sync-production-environment`)
3. **Workflow deploys to Railway `production` environment** → Creates if missing, triggers deployment from commit

### Dev (dev branch)
1. **Push to dev** → Vercel creates preview deployment
2. **Vercel deployment succeeds** → GitHub Actions workflow triggers (`sync-dev-environment`)
3. **Workflow deploys to Railway `dev` environment** → Creates if missing, triggers deployment from commit

### Pull Requests
1. **PR is opened** → Vercel creates preview deployment + Neon creates database branch
2. **Vercel deployment succeeds** → GitHub Actions workflow triggers (`sync-preview-environment`)
3. **Workflow checks for Railway PR environment** → Creates `pr-{number}` if missing (duplicated from production)
4. **Workflow sets API_URL** → Only variable modified, others inherited from production
5. **Railway deploys from commit** → Realtime service fetches other config via discovery endpoint
6. **PR is closed** → Workflow deletes the Railway PR environment

## Environment Management

### Creation Strategy

The workflow **manually creates** Railway environments instead of relying on Railway's automatic PR environment feature:

- **New PR**: Duplicates production environment, sets `API_URL`, triggers deploy
- **Subsequent deploys**: Updates `API_URL` only, triggers redeploy
- **PR closed**: Deletes the environment via Railway API

### Variable Strategy

Only `API_URL` is set via the workflow. All other variables are:

1. **Inherited from production** when environment is duplicated
2. **Fetched via discovery endpoint** at runtime for dynamic values (DATABASE_URL, etc.)

## Required Secrets

Add these secrets to your GitHub repository (run `pnpm github:setup` to automate):

| Secret | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| `RAILWAY_TOKEN` | Railway **team** token (from team settings or railway.app/account/tokens) |
| `RAILWAY_PROJECT_ID` | Railway project ID (from project settings) |
| `RAILWAY_SERVICE_ID` | Railway realtime service ID |
| `VERCEL_TOKEN` | Vercel API token (from vercel.com/account/tokens) |
| `VERCEL_ORG_ID` | Vercel org/team ID (auto-set from `.vercel/project.json`) |

**Note**: The workflow uses a team token to dynamically create temporary project tokens for each deployment. This allows deploying to any environment while keeping security tight - project tokens are created, used for `railway up`, and immediately deleted.

## Railway Configuration

### railway.json

The `apps/realtime/railway.json` file configures Railway builds:

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://railway.com/railway.schema.json",
  "build": {
    "builder": "NIXPACKS",
    "buildCommand": "pnpm install --frozen-lockfile && pnpm --filter @app/realtime build"
  },
  "deploy": {
    "startCommand": "pnpm --filter @app/realtime start",
    "healthcheckPath": "/",
    "healthcheckTimeout": 300,
    "restartPolicyType": "ON_FAILURE"
  }
}
```

### Production Environment Variables

Set these in Railway dashboard for the production environment (they will be copied to PR environments):

```
REDIS_URL                        # Shared Redis instance
REALTIME_SECRET_KEY              # Same across all environments
WS_PORT                          # Default: 3001
TCP_PORT                         # Default: 9000
ALLOWED_ORIGINS                  # Include *.vercel.app
API_URL                          # Production URL (overridden per PR)
VERCEL_AUTOMATION_BYPASS_SECRET  # Required if Vercel deployment protection is enabled
```

### Vercel Deployment Protection Bypass

If your Vercel project has deployment protection enabled (standard/password/Vercel auth), the realtime service's discovery requests will be blocked. To bypass this:

1. Go to Vercel Dashboard → Project Settings → Deployment Protection
2. Scroll to "Protection Bypass for Automation"
3. Copy the bypass secret
4. Add `VERCEL_AUTOMATION_BYPASS_SECRET` to Railway production environment

The discovery request will automatically include the bypass token as query parameters.

## GitHub Actions Workflow

The workflow (`.github/workflows/preview-realtime.yml`) handles:

### Sync Job (on deployment_status success)

1. **Get PR number** from commit SHA or branch name
2. **Get Vercel preview URL** from deployment event
3. **Check for existing PR environment** in Railway
4. **Create environment if missing** by duplicating from production
5. **Set API_URL** to Vercel preview URL
6. **Trigger redeploy** of the service
7. **Comment on PR** with preview links

### Cleanup Job (on pull_request closed)

1. **Find PR environment** by name (`pr-{number}`)
2. **Delete environment** via Railway API

### Manual Sync Script

If automatic sync fails, run manually:

```bash
export RAILWAY_TOKEN="your-railway-team-token"

# Create or update PR environment
node .github/scripts/railway-preview-sync.mjs \
  --project-id "railway-project-id" \
  --service-id "railway-service-id" \
  --pr-number "123" \
  --api-url "https://your-preview.vercel.app" \
  --action "upsert"

# Delete PR environment
node .github/scripts/railway-preview-sync.mjs \
  --project-id "railway-project-id" \
  --pr-number "123" \
  --action "delete"

# Deploy to named environment
node .github/scripts/railway-preview-sync.mjs \
  --project-id "railway-project-id" \
  --service-id "railway-service-id" \
  --environment "production" \
  --api-url "https://your-app.vercel.app" \
  --action "deploy"
```

The script uses a hybrid approach:
1. Uses the Railway GraphQL API to manage environments and variables
2. Creates a temporary project token for the target environment
3. Deploys using `railway up` with that token
4. Deletes the temporary token after deployment

## Setup Checklist

### Vercel + Neon

1. [ ] Install Neon integration in Vercel project settings
2. [ ] Enable "Create a branch for each preview deployment"

### Railway

1. [ ] Set production environment variables (REDIS_URL, REALTIME_SECRET_KEY, etc.)
2. [ ] Add `*.vercel.app` to ALLOWED_ORIGINS
3. [ ] Deploy with `apps/realtime/railway.json`
4. [ ] **Do NOT enable** Railway's automatic PR environments (workflow manages this)
5. [ ] **Disconnect GitHub autodeploys**: Go to Service Settings → Source → click "Disconnect" to prevent Railway from auto-deploying on commits (the CI workflow handles deployments via API)

### GitHub

Run `pnpm github:setup` or manually add:

1. [ ] Add `RAILWAY_TOKEN` secret (team token from team settings)
2. [ ] Add `RAILWAY_PROJECT_ID` secret
3. [ ] Add `RAILWAY_SERVICE_ID` secret
4. [ ] Add `VERCEL_TOKEN` secret (created from team context)
5. [ ] Add `VERCEL_ORG_ID` secret (auto-populated from `.vercel/project.json`)

## Troubleshooting

### Environment Creation Failed

1. Check RAILWAY_TOKEN has permissions to create environments
2. Verify production environment exists and is named "production" or "prod"
3. Check Railway API logs for detailed errors

### API_URL Not Updating

1. Check Vercel preview URL is being fetched correctly
2. Verify RAILWAY_TOKEN has write permissions
3. Check service ID matches the realtime service

### Environment Not Deleted

1. Check PR environment naming matches `pr-{number}` pattern
2. Verify RAILWAY_TOKEN has delete permissions
3. Check if environment was manually renamed

### CORS Issues in Preview

Ensure `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` in Railway production includes:
- `https://*.vercel.app`
- Or the specific preview URL pattern for your project

### Discovery Returns HTML / Authentication Page

If the discovery endpoint returns an HTML authentication page instead of JSON:

1. Vercel deployment protection is enabled
2. Add `VERCEL_AUTOMATION_BYPASS_SECRET` to Railway environment
3. Get the secret from Vercel Dashboard → Project Settings → Deployment Protection → Protection Bypass for Automation

### Duplicate Railway Deployments

If Railway deploys twice for each commit:

1. Railway's GitHub autodeploy is enabled (auto-deploys on every commit)
2. The CI workflow is also triggering a deploy via CLI
3. **Fix**: Go to Railway Dashboard → Service Settings → Source → click "Disconnect"
4. This stops Railway from auto-deploying; the CI workflow will handle deployments via `railway redeploy`

### Skipped/Cascading GitHub Actions Jobs

If you see many skipped workflow runs after each push:

1. Other services (like Railway) may also fire `deployment_status` events
2. The workflow now filters on `github.actor == 'vercel[bot]'` to only run for Vercel deployments
3. Non-Vercel deployments are ignored at the job level (not skipped, just filtered out)

## Flow Examples

### Production Deployment (main branch)
```
Push to main
  │
  └─► Vercel deploys → https://project.vercel.app (Production)
        │
        └─► GitHub Actions triggers (deployment_status success, environment=Production)
              │
              ├─► Finds Railway "production" environment (or creates if missing)
              │
              ├─► Sets API_URL = production Vercel URL
              │
              └─► Triggers deployment from commit SHA
                    └─► Realtime service fetches config via discovery
```

### Dev Deployment (dev branch)
```
Push to dev
  │
  └─► Vercel deploys → https://project-dev.vercel.app (Preview)
        │
        └─► GitHub Actions triggers (deployment_status success, ref=dev)
              │
              ├─► Finds Railway "dev" environment (or creates if missing)
              │
              ├─► Sets API_URL = dev Vercel URL
              │
              └─► Triggers deployment from commit SHA
                    └─► Realtime service fetches config via discovery
```

### PR Deployment
```
PR #42 opened
  │
  └─► Vercel deploys → https://project-git-feature-42.vercel.app (Preview)
        │
        └─► GitHub Actions triggers (deployment_status success)
              │
              ├─► No Railway pr-42 environment exists
              │     └─► Creates pr-42 by duplicating production
              │
              ├─► Sets API_URL = https://project-git-feature-42.vercel.app
              │
              └─► Triggers deployment from commit SHA
                    └─► Realtime service fetches config via discovery

PR #42 closed
  │
  └─► GitHub Actions triggers (pull_request closed)
        │
        └─► Deletes pr-42 environment from Railway
```
